 exit，export 是出口贸易。","砍价要用完整问句。","Mr. Wang 是第三人称单数，be 动词要用 is。"};
        public static readonly string[] EnglishReasonEn={"Agree is a verb, so it cannot follow am very.","Welcome to is followed directly by the place.","You lose your way, not your road.","Execution can mean putting someone to death; use under construction.","The fire-escape door is called an emergency exit.","The natural phrase is watch your step.","Noisy is an adjective; the sign should ask for quiet.","Nobody loses a foot; metro signs say Mind the gap.","Beware of means avoid, so it says the opposite.","A literal dish name is scary; describe the ingredients.","Hong shao means braised, and the lion head is a big meatball.","It means so-so; there are no horses or tigers.","It means for your sake; face is not something you hand over.","After please, an imperative uses the base form shut, not shutting.","Remember to is followed by the base form take, not taking.","Knowledge is usually gained, not learned.","English does not say play computer.","Books are read, not looked.","Photos are taken, not made.","Boring describes the cause; you feel bored.","People feel excited; things are exciting.","Although and but are not used together.","Because and so are not used together.","English questions start with how do you.","Discuss takes an object directly, without about.","Marry takes the person directly.","Return already means come back.","Reach takes the place directly.","Information is uncountable.","Homework is uncountable.","Advice is uncountable.","Furniture is uncountable.","People is already plural.","Past events need the past tense went.","Third person singular takes doesn't.","The present continuous needs studying.","English says on the internet.","Listen needs to before its object.","Explain something to someone, not explain someone.","Lend means give; borrow means take.","Prices are high; things are expensive.","Baths are taken, not washed.","Just say call; hit a phone is literal.","You take a bus; sit is literal.","Pain is a noun; say hurts.","The literal internet slang makes no sense in English.","It means we are very close; the literal version is meaningless.","Signs say free admission.","Signs simply say No smoking.","Keep needs the state closed.","It means only staff may enter.","Are stolen means you yourself were taken.","It means feeling anxious.","It just means very funny; die is literal and alarming.","It needs a cup of coffee.","Go shopping takes no to the.","Say the battery is dead.","Computers get viruses, not poison.","It is a red packet or red envelope.","It means scrolling, not brushing.","It means teaming up in a game.","It needs add me as a friend.","Watch out needs for before the danger.","Children is plural; use child.","The perfect question begins with have.","The continuous form needs going.","Home is an adverb here; no to.","Phones are turned off, not closed.","Just say my first time here.","It means overjoyed, not angry.","Prepaid phones run out of credit.","The item is a package, not an express.","English has its own matching proverb.","Cheap is an adjective, not a verb.","The natural phrase is across the hall.","Age needs years old or just the number.","Don't takes the base form throw, not throws.","Export means trade; the door is an exit.","Bargaining needs a full question.","Mr. Wang is a singular third-person subject, so use is."};
