        public static readonly string[] CompareGoodEn={"Note the error code and restart; if it repeats, check drivers and RAM.","Try rolling back to the old driver in Device Manager.","Depends: 8 GB is fine for daily use; 16 GB helps big games and editing.","Make it long, mix letters, numbers and symbols, and don't reuse it.","Keep at least two copies, e.g. an external drive plus cloud storage.","Disable unneeded startup programs and clean up the disk.","Maybe dust or heavy load. Clean it and check Task Manager.","Cracks often carry viruses and break the law. Use legit or free software.","Check the Recycle Bin; if not there, stop writing and try recovery tools.","Back up important files first and check software compatibility.","From the official site, such as NVIDIA's or AMD's.","Clear temporary files and move big files to another drive.","Unplug it, turn it upside down, let it dry fully, then test.","First check the monitor's power cable and video cable.","Soft noise is normal; odd clicking means back up your data now.","A drive that stores data in flash memory. Faster and quieter.","Confirm by phone or in person first. Don't rush to transfer.","Don't. It may be phishing. Use official channels instead.","Don't share it. Real customer service never asks for codes.","Meet in a busy public place by day, and tell your family.","Better not. Public networks can be snooped; use mobile data.","Don't pay privately. Trades inside the platform are protected.","Probably a fake ad. Close it and scan with your own antivirus.","No. ID details can be misused. Protect your privacy.","Check via the courier's official site or phone. Don't click.","Not advised. Sleep helps memory; just review key points.","Outline first: intro, a few key points, conclusion. Then write.","Log them, note why you erred, and redo them a few days later.","Put the phone away, focus for 25 minutes, then take a break.","Understand the meaning and imagery, read aloud, learn line by line.","I can help plan and 